  "why_this_file_exists": "The authority resolves a registration's commissioning_digest against authorisations delivered to it through the commissioning path, never presented by the device. Whether a registration is applied, retained pending, or refused therefore depends on what the authority already holds, which no single wire artifact can express. Each case names the held state, the arriving artifact and its source, and the outcome the contract requires. The artifacts reuse the published registration and authorisation vectors so a verifier that already reproduces those bytes needs nothing new to sign; one registration is newly signed with the published device seed so that a resolved authorisation naming another key can be exercised.",
  "resolution_order": [
    "parses",
    "key_selection",
    "signature",
    "recompute_epoch_and_key_id",
    "resolve_commissioning_digest",
    "apply"
  ],
